---
import Section from '../Section.astro';

const outcomes = [
  'Less manual work',
  'Better visibility',
  'More reliable systems',
  'Clearer decisions',
  'Fewer fragile handoffs',
  'Greater operating capacity',
  'Measurable improvement in the business',
];
---

<Section variant="white" id="why-guava" label="Why Guava">
  <h2 class="text-h2 mb-md max-w-3xl">
    Technology should serve the business&nbsp;&mdash; not the other way around.
  </h2>
  <p class="text-muted max-w-2xl mb-lg">
    Guava starts with the required operational outcome. We do not begin with a
    preferred technology. Success should look like:
  </p>

  <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-lg gap-y-sm max-w-3xl list-none p-0 mb-lg">
    {outcomes.map((item) => (
      <li class="flex items-start gap-sm">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand"></span>
        <span class="text-body text-muted">{item}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-text">
    Technology is useful only when it produces those outcomes.
  </p>
</Section>